{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The people bring much.</b> The word מרבים indicates that they did not cease from bringing. And Scripture tells you of a great virtue in the voluntary offering of all Israel, the men and the women: for the men volunteered the silver and the copper and the blue and the purple and the crimson worm, and the women volunteered their gold ornaments. The principal of all this offering they brought on the first day to Mosheh, for so the language of the pericah indicates by the expression of haste, as in the phrase ״ויצאו כל עדת בני ישראל ויבאו״, and moreover what Scripture says: ״והם הביאו אליו עוד נדבה בבקר בבקר״." "<b>And the meaning</b> of this is that after they brought the principal of all the offering on that day, there still remained among them a few who brought him an offering בבקר בבקר, that is to say, on the morrow, early in the morning. And Scripture reveals to us the virtue of the wise men who did the work in their great faithfulness, for they reported this to Mosheh — and they were busy and engaged in their labor yet left off their work to tell Mosheh, for thus the phrase איש איש ממלאכתו אשר המה עושים indicates; and this is the sense of ״ויאמרו אל משה לאמר״ — saying time after time. And also the virtue of Mosheh who ruled over them, that he did not choose their silver and their gold, and therefore it is written ״ויצו משה ויעבירו קול במחנה״ to put a stop to the matter."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:37.179490526Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}